@startuml seq_sft_engage_standstill
title SC-SFT-01 - Drive engagement N / P -> D at standstill

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-SFT-006, SYS-ACT-001, SYS-SEL-001, SYS-SEL-005, SIM-PLT-002, SIM-CON-002
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

note over TCU: mode Normal, vehicle at standstill (< 2 km/h);\nin P / N the TCU prepares 1st: SS_A = ON, SS_B = ON (SYS-SEL-005)

alt starting from P
  User -> Console : press the brake, select D
  note right of Console: leaving P needs SLS = ON (brake pressed,\nstandstill), see SC-SEL-03
else starting from N
  User -> Console : select D
end
Console -> Plant : selector D
Plant -> Plant : lever in D: engages 1st from SS_A = ON, SS_B = ON (SIM-PLT-002)
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 3 (D)
... 50 ms unchanged (SYS-SEL-001) ...
TCU -> TCU : D selected at standstill -> command 1st gear (SYS-SFT-006)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = ON, SS_B = ON (1st, SYS-ACT-001), PCS_Duty from the table
note right of TCU: pattern unchanged, no shift
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: SelectorState = 3 (D), GearTarget = 1, Mode = 0 (Normal)

User -> Console : release the brake, throttle
Console -> Plant : Brake = released, Throttle
Plant -> Plant : vehicle accelerates in 1st (SIM-PLT-006)
note over Plant, TCU: upshifts continue in SC-SFT-03
@enduml
